%I A401221 #27 Nov 14 2026 22:00:34
%S A401221 1,12,6,2,18,12,6,12,12,6,6,12,24,6,12,12,24,12,12,2,12,6,24,6,12,24,
%T A401221 12,6,24,12,12,24,6,12,24,24,18,12,12,24,12,12,36,24,12,18,12,24,12,
%U A401221 48,2,36,24,12,12,42,6,12,24,12,12,36,12,24,72,12,24,12,48
%N A401221 Sizes of the successive shells of the hexagonal close-packed (HCP) lattice, centered on a lattice point.
%C A401221 The HCP structure is a non-Bravais lattice formed by an alternating ABAB... stacking of triangular A_2 sheets with an ideal height-to-base ratio c/L = sqrt(8/3).
%C A401221 Points in the HCP structure have Cartesian coordinates (x, y, z) = (L*(u + s + (v + t)/2), L*sqrt(3)*(v + t)/2, L*k*sqrt(2/3)), where u, v, k are integers, and L is the lattice parameter. Here (s, t) = (0, 0) for even k (A-layers), and (s, t) = (1/3, 1/3) for odd k (B-layers).
%C A401221 Scaling the squared Euclidean distance by 3 eliminates irrational axial spacing and yields a scaled squared distance metric D = 3*(R/L)^2. This reduces the boundary condition to the following ternary Diophantine inequalities for integer triples (u, v, k):
%C A401221 D = 3*(u^2 + u*v + v^2) + 2*k^2 <= 3*(R/L)^2 for even k;
%C A401221 D = 3*(u^2 + u*v + v^2 + u + v) + 1 + 2*k^2 <= 3*(R/L)^2 for odd k.
%C A401221 The shell counts at a given metric D can be expressed as a linear combination of four positive-definite integral ternary theta series. Let H(q) = Sum_{D>=0} N(D)*q^D be the generating function for the number of HCP sites N(D) at metric D. Let A(q) = Sum_{u,v in Z} q^(u^2 + u*v + v^2) and T(q) = Sum_{k in Z} q^(k^2). Then 2*H(q) = A(q)*T(q^2) - A(q^3)*T(q^2) - A(q)*T(q^8) + 3*A(q^3)*T(q^8). (This theta-series formulation was contributed by _Alper Ferudun_, derived from the enumeration script).
%C A401221 This sequence gives the nonzero terms of the HCP theta series A004012, where the valid metrics D are cataloged in A005870 = {0, 3, 6, 8, 9, 11, 12, ...}.
%C A401221 While A007899 gives the coordination sequence of the HCP structure considered as an infinite regular graph (shortest graph-hop distance), A401221 gives the exact physical counts on successive Euclidean metric shells of radius R centered on a lattice site.
%C A401221 Differs from the FCC metric shells (nonzero terms of theta series A004015) starting at the third non-origin shell (index n = 3). For FCC, the first two shells have 12 points and 6 points, followed by 24 points. For HCP, the shell of 6 points is followed by an axial shell of only 2 points due to the axial layer truncation.
%D A401221 J. H. Conway and N. J. A. Sloane, Sphere Packings, Lattices and Groups, Springer-Verlag, 3rd ed., 1999.
%H A401221 Andrew J. Morris, <a href="/A401221/b401221.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%H A401221 Andrew J. Morris, <a href="/A401221/a401221.txt">C++ engine A401221</a>.
%F A401221 a(n) = A400434(n) - A400434(n-1) for n >= 1; a(0) = 1.
%F A401221 a(n) = A004012(A005870(n)).
%e A401221 The first few shells and individual shell counts are:
%e A401221 n = 0: D = 0, R = 0, origin atom, a(0) = 1.
%e A401221 n = 1: D = 3, R = 1, 12 kissing spheres (6 in-plane at k=0, 3 in layer k=1, 3 in layer k=-1), a(1) = 12.
%e A401221 n = 2: D = 6, R = sqrt(2), 6 second neighbors (3 in layer k=1, 3 in layer k=-1), a(2) = 6.
%e A401221 n = 3: D = 8, R = sqrt(8/3), 2 axial neighbors at k=+-2, a(3) = 2.
%e A401221 n = 4: D = 9, R = sqrt(3), 18 neighbors (6 in-plane at k=0, 6 in layer k=1, 6 in layer k=-1), a(4) = 18.
%e A401221 n = 5: D = 11, R = sqrt(11/3), 12 neighbors (6 in layer k=2, 6 in layer k=-2), a(5) = 12.
%e A401221 n = 6: D = 12, R = 2, 6 in-plane neighbors at k=0, a(6) = 6.
%o A401221 (C++) // See Links.
%Y A401221 Cf. A004012, A004015, A005870, A007202, A007899, A400434.
